# Hardware

The XMPL100's pins, timing and power, as the driver uses them.

## Pins

| Pin | Direction | Function |
| --- | --- | --- |
| VDD | Power | Supply; 100 nF to GND at the pin |
| GND | Power | |
| OUT | Out | Open drain, active low: asserted above the trip point and during the self-test pulse. Needs a pull-up |
| SHDN_N | In | Shutdown, active low; optional (`CtrlPin::Enable`) |

There is no data bus: the driver reads OUT through `GpioRead(InPin::Out, ...)` and drives SHDN_N through the
optional `GpioSet()`. Your port maps the logical levels to the pins: `GpioSignal::ACTIVE` on OUT is a low level.

## Timing

| Parameter | Symbol | Value | Driver |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Trip point | T_TRIP | 85 °C typical | `kTripPointC` |
| Shutdown reset time | t_SD | 10 µs minimum | `kShutdownTimeUs` |
| Self-test pulse | t_POST | 500 µs minimum, 2 ms maximum | `kSelfTestTimeMinUs`, `kSelfTestTimeMaxUs`; sampled at `kSelfTestCheckUs` |

